  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "L1 gold records for transferable reference contexts report absolute oral bioavailability values of 48–82% (diclofenac ~50%, alfuzosin 49%, etoposide 48–57%, lumiracoxib 74%, brotizolam 70%, BI 425809 71.6%, indomethacin SR 76–80%, suvorexant 82%), all above the 20% threshold; these are the strongest endpoint evidence and support a high prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C04","C05","C06","C09","C12","C14","C29","C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 C225 shows a reference molecule (BMS-2) containing the same N-(3-methyl-5-chloroisoxazol-4-yl)sulfonamide group as the query lost only 5.9% of parent after 5 min in human liver microsomes, indicating that this key moiety is not rapidly cleared and supporting a high prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C225"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 C249/C226 report HLM intrinsic clearance of 137 µL/min/mg for DS-1971a, yet the L1 gold context for BI 425809/iclepertin gives absolute F 71.6%, demonstrating that high intrinsic clearance alone does not establish F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C249","C226","C02","C36"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 high-clearance isoxazole-sulfonamide analogs (C242, C239) and benzodioxole-containing clearance records (C248, C213, C252, C253) are mechanistically relevant but lack oral F outcomes and are structurally distant from the query; they do not affirm F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C242","C239","C248","C213","C252","C253"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C225","C249","C226","C241","C242","C239","C252","C253","C215","C257","C222","C211","C245","C223","C216","C224","C254","C248","C213","C258","C236","C227","C247","C230","C260","C250","C219","C229","C259","C256","C217","C228","C233","C218","C231","C234","C237","C238","C243","C244","C251","C255","C220","C212","C240","C246","C221","C232","C235","C214"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability experiment is available; L6 records concern reference molecules.",
    "No query-specific intestinal absorption, permeability, solubility, or efflux measurement is available.",
    "The relative contributions of benzodioxole demethylenation, isoxazole-sulfonamide metabolism, and thiophene ketone clearance to query first-pass loss are unquantified.",
    "Formulation, dose, and prandial-state effects on query exposure are unknown."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because transferable L1 absolute-bioavailability outcomes (48–82%) and L6 metabolic-stability context (close isoxazole-sulfonamide analog stable; high intrinsic clearance in another sulfonamide analog coexisting with 71.6% F) support the threshold, while no affirmative query-specific low-F evidence exists. L6 hepatic-clearance records are mixed and mostly lack oral F outcomes, so they do not overturn the prior decision; ionization/TPSA concerns remain uncertainties, not affirmative low evidence."
}

